# Medical Exam Human Documentation Governance

## Gold Standard gate (required)

Every Medical Exam chief complaint template remediation must pass **both**:

1. **Structural Gold Standard / Track C** — MDM.1 coverage, i18n parity, prohibited key tokens, cannot-miss differentials.
2. **Human Documentation Audit** — rendered EN chip text is paste-ready emergency physician documentation.

**Not one or the other. Both.**

Applies to: ME.2V-R, ME.2W-R, ME.2Y-R, ME.2Z-R, ME.2AA-R, ME.2X-R, ME.2AB-R, ENTERPRISE-CLEANUP, and all future Medical Exam chief complaint remediation phases.

## Core rule

Every sticky-note chip must render **chart-ready, human-sounding clinician documentation**. The provider must be able to click any chip and paste the rendered text into the chart **without editing**.

## Required human documentation checks

- No workflow language (`discussed`, `recommended`, `advised`, `if indicated`)
- No governance / meta-documentation language (`historian used`, `assessment completed`, `exam completed`, `evaluation completed`)
- No internal terminology (`chip`, `sticky note`, `fragment`, `template`, `governance`, `workflow`)
- No chip terminology leaking into rendered values
- No `reviewed` outside **mdmDataReviewed** (diagnostic review phrases only)
- No `assessed` outside clinically valid physical-exam phrasing when truly needed
- No `considered`
- No `historian used`
- No `if documented` / `if given` / `if performed`
- No noun-chain return precautions
- Must read naturally when rendered
- Must be paste-ready clinician documentation

## Section-specific rules

| Section | Rule |
|---------|------|
| HPI / ROS / Exam / Reassessment | Clinical facts only; no review/assessment meta-language |
| mdmWorkingAssessment / Impression | Working diagnosis language (`suspected`, `low suspicion for`, `concern for`) |
| mdmDifferentialSynthesis | Diagnosis names, not `considered` |
| mdmDataReviewed | **Only** section where `reviewed` is allowed (`CBC reviewed`, `CT reviewed`, etc.) |
| mdmRiskStratification | Risk framing (`low risk; …`, `high risk for …`), not stub tokens |
| mdmClinicalRationale | Clinical reasoning, not process documentation |
| Plan / Disposition | Actions and instructions (`given`, `arranged`, `encouraged`), not `discussed` / `recommended` |

## FAIL examples (rendered values)

- `nausea today reviewed`
- `fever reviewed`
- `abdominal pain reviewed`
- `exam completed`
- `assessment completed`
- `hydration status assessed`
- `differential considered`
- `specialist consult if indicated`
- `caregiver historian used`
- `return lethargy breathing dehydration fever`
- `pediatrician follow-up recommended`
- `return precautions discussed`

## PASS examples (rendered values)

- `nausea began today`
- `multiple episodes of vomiting`
- `unable to tolerate oral intake`
- `fever began yesterday`
- `reported Tmax 102°F at home`
- `abdomen soft and non-tender`
- `hydration improved after treatment`
- `low suspicion for meningitis`
- `parent at bedside`
- `return for lethargy, difficulty breathing, dehydration, or persistent fever`
- `CBC reviewed` (mdmDataReviewed only)

## Sample rendering requirement

For each registered template, generate **≥ 20 deterministic rendered note samples** including all sections:

HPI, ROS+, ROS−, Exam, Reassessment, MDM Working Assessment, MDM Differential, MDM Data Reviewed, MDM Risk Stratification, MDM Reasoning, Clinical Impression, Plan, Disposition.

Each sample must pass: *Would an emergency physician sign this note without editing the generated text?*

## Implementation

- Governance module: `apps/web/src/lib/providerDocumentationHumanDocumentationAudit.ts`
- Permanent test gate: `apps/web/src/lib/providerDocumentationHumanDocumentationAudit.test.ts`
- Register new families in `HUMAN_DOCUMENTATION_AUDIT_FAMILIES`
- Run: `pnpm --filter @medora/web exec vitest run src/lib/providerDocumentationHumanDocumentationAudit.test.ts`

## Required remediation report sections

Every Medical Exam remediation report must include:

1. Repo readiness audit
2. Discovery table
3. Scope decision
4. Files changed
5. HPI summary
6. ROS summary
7. Physical exam summary
8. Reassessment summary
9. MDM reinforcement summary
10. Cannot-miss coverage
11. **Human Documentation Audit result**
12. **Rendered sample note result**
13. Track C result
14. MDM.1 verification
15. Governance result
16. Compatibility audit result
17. Verification results
18. Migration assessment
19. Exact unstaged file list
20. Suggested commit message
